{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117732","id":3430969516,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7MgHCs","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117732","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117732.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117732.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117732","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117732/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117732/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117732/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/73b3f4cc38ab7be6d4712c2b60db40e67dde9cd8","number":117732,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"SceneTree: Replace manual thread checks with ERR_MAIN_THREAD_GUARD","user":{"login":"itsharsh234","id":168270885,"node_id":"U_kgDOCgecJQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/168270885?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsharsh234","html_url":"https://github.com/itsharsh234","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsharsh234/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsharsh234/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsharsh234/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsharsh234/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsharsh234/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsharsh234/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsharsh234/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsharsh234/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsharsh234/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# PR: SceneTree: Replace manual thread checks with ERR_MAIN_THREAD_GUARD\r\n \r\n---\r\n \r\n## Summary\r\n \r\nThis PR completes the migration of `scene_tree.cpp` from ad-hoc\r\n`ERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(!Thread::is_main_thread(), ...)` checks to the\r\ncanonical `ERR_MAIN_THREAD_GUARD` / `ERR_MAIN_THREAD_GUARD_V` macros\r\nestablished in #75901. It also adds guards to two functions that had\r\n**no thread check at all** despite mutating main-thread-only state.\r\n \r\nNo logic is changed. This is a pure consistency and correctness cleanup.\r\n \r\n---\r\n \r\n## Motivation\r\n \r\nPR #75901 introduced `ERR_MAIN_THREAD_GUARD` as the standard way to\r\nenforce main-thread-only access in Godot. The macro:\r\n \r\n- Is a no-op in release builds (zero runtime cost in shipping games).\r\n- Uses thread-local storage for the check — faster than a raw\r\n  `Thread::is_main_thread()` call.\r\n- Produces a uniform, identifiable error message that tooling and\r\n  contributors can grep for.\r\n- Makes the threading contract of each function self-documenting at\r\n  the call site.\r\n \r\n`scene_tree.cpp` was only partially updated. Several functions still\r\nused the old pattern, and two were missing guards entirely, meaning\r\ncalling them from a worker thread would silently corrupt state in\r\nrelease builds.\r\n \r\n---\r\n \r\n## Changes\r\n \r\n### Functions migrated from old pattern → ERR_MAIN_THREAD_GUARD\r\n \r\n| Function | Old check |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `quit()` | `_THREAD_SAFE_METHOD_` only (mutex, not identity check) |\r\n| `set_pause()` | `ERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(!Thread::is_main_thread(), ...)` |\r\n| `set_suspend()` | `ERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(!Thread::is_main_thread(), ...)` |\r\n| `set_current_scene()` | `ERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(!Thread::is_main_thread(), ...)` |\r\n| `change_scene_to_file()` | `ERR_FAIL_COND_V_MSG(!Thread::is_main_thread(), ...)` |\r\n| `reload_current_scene()` | `ERR_FAIL_COND_V_MSG(!Thread::is_main_thread(), ...)` |\r\n| `unload_current_scene()` | `ERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(!Thread::is_main_thread(), ...)` |\r\n| `add_current_scene()` | `ERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(!Thread::is_main_thread(), ...)` |\r\n| `set_multiplayer()` | `ERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(!Thread::is_main_thread(), ...)` |\r\n| `get_multiplayer()` | `ERR_FAIL_COND_V_MSG(!Thread::is_main_thread(), ...)` |\r\n| `set_multiplayer_poll_enabled()` | `ERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(!Thread::is_main_thread(), ...)` |\r\n \r\n### Functions with missing guards — newly added\r\n \r\n| Function | Reason |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `change_scene_to_packed()` | Mutates `current_scene` and calls `instantiate()` — main-thread only, had no check |\r\n| `change_scene_to_node()` | Mutates `pending_new_scene_id`, `prev_scene_id`, calls `root->remove_child()` — main-thread only, had no check |\r\n \r\n---\r\n \r\n## What was NOT changed\r\n \r\n- All `_THREAD_SAFE_METHOD_` mutex guards are preserved where they\r\n  already exist — they serve a different purpose (protecting data\r\n  accessed from both threads) and are complementary to the identity\r\n  guards, not a replacement.\r\n- No logic, no algorithm, no data structure was modified.\r\n- No new includes or dependencies were added.\r\n \r\n---\r\n \r\n## Testing\r\n \r\n- Confirm that calling any of the above functions from a\r\n  `Thread` or a `PROCESS_THREAD_GROUP_SUB_THREAD` node emits the\r\n  expected error in debug builds and returns early.\r\n- Confirm no regression in normal (main-thread) usage by running the\r\n  existing scene-change and multiplayer test projects.\r\n \r\n---\r\n \r\n## Related\r\n \r\n- #75901 — original `ERR_MAIN_THREAD_GUARD` introduction by reduz\r\n\r\n\r\n## AI Assisted \r\n- I have made this pull request with the help of **AI**  . Specifically **Claude** . I have reviewed and edited the code and have performed the necessary checks before making this pull request \r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"arc